  "notes": [
    "Symmetry octant: normal translation plus the two in-plane rotation components restrained on x=0, theta=0 and theta=pi/2; the two cross-section translations restrained on the diaphragm ring x=300 (axial u free).",
    "The deflection sequence is non-monotone: the error reaches 0.17% at N=16 and then rises (1.28% at N=24, 1.82% at N=32, 2.37% at N=48).  N=16 is an accidental cancellation of two competing discretisation errors, not the converged answer; the extrapolated limit of the fine rungs is the honest estimate of the discrete limit.",
    "The point force is singular; the deflection at the load point is therefore not mesh independent in the classical sense.  Both an algebraic and a logarithmic asymptotic model are fitted to the fine rungs and both are reported, so the reader can judge which regularisation the ladder is following.",
    "The pinched cylinder has no closed form; its only oracle is a converged numerical value, so the asymptotic offset of this formulation is reported as a formulation characteristic rather than hidden."
  ]
